Agent: Tropical Pineapple‑Mango Punch (non‑alcoholic) — yields about 12–16 (8‑oz) servings

Ingredients
- 6 cups (48 fl oz) pineapple juice  
- 3 cups (24 fl oz) mango nectar  
- 2 cups (16 fl oz) orange juice  
- 1 cup (8 fl oz) passion fruit juice  
- 1/2 cup (4 fl oz) fresh lime juice (about 4 limes)  
- 1/2 cup (4 fl oz) grenadine  
- 1 liter (about 34 fl oz) chilled ginger ale  
- 1 pineapple, peeled and sliced into rings or chunks (for garnish)  
- 2 oranges, thinly sliced (for garnish)  
- Ice

Instructions
1. In a large pitcher or beverage dispenser, combine pineapple juice, mango nectar, orange juice, passion fruit juice, fresh lime juice, and grenadine. Stir until blended.  
2. Chill the mixture for at least 2 hours (or up to 24 hours).  
3. Just before serving, add the chilled ginger ale and gently stir to combine.  
4. Add ice to the dispenser or individual glasses, then float pineapple rings and orange slices on top for garnish. Serve immediately.  

Make‑ahead note: Mix the juices and grenadine and refrigerate up to 24 hours; add ginger ale and ice right before guests arrive to keep the punch fizzy.
